---
title: Kleftiko v1
description: Classic Greek very slow-cooked lamb
source: https://www.mydish.co.uk/recipe/8851/annie-bell-s-slow-slow-kleftiko
author: Annie Bell
image: https://cdn.biteq.uk/members/257881/201061171423766-913661-656489-676995.jpg
servings: 6
course: Main
prep time: 15m
cook time: 5h20m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Greek
tags:
- savoury
- main-course
- meat
- greek
---

Preheat oven to 140°C. Prepare two long sheets of baking paper and a #roasting dish{} that will hold the lamb comfortably.

Heat a #large frying pan{} over a medium-high heat. Lightly cover the @lamb shoulder{2.25%kg} in @olive oil{}, season with @sea salt{} and @black pepper{} and sear to cover it all over.

Lay the two sheets of baking paper on top of each other at right angles. Allow enough either side to enclose the lamb in a loose parcel with some air inside and for pleating the edges together two or three times.

Scatter half the @fresh oregano{small bunch} in the centre of the paper. Drizzle over a little @olive oil{} and place the lamb on top. Dust with @ground cinnamon{0.5%tsp}. Pick the leaves off the remaining oregano and scatter these over. Scatter the @garlic{2%heads}(separated into cloves) over and around. Drizzle over some @olive oil{}, pour over the @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and then seal the parcel by pleating the opposite sides together (brushing the edges with a little @?egg white{1} will help to give a good seal).

Place the parcel in a roasting dish and roast for ~{5%hours} until the meat is meltingly tender. Skim any excess fat from the juices before serving.